{#- targum Connect: targum in Claude, ChatGPT and the other assistants (targum-internal#80,
    remade 2026-09-24 to stand beside the front door).

    A public page, so §6 says it sells: lead with what the reader gets, in their words.
    Most people who land here have not met targum at all, so the page says what targum is
    before it says how to add it, and shows the conversation before it lists the steps.

    **Note 2 is still the design of the steps: assume it is their first install.** Every
    app has its own tab with its own steps, and nothing is detected or guessed. The tabs
    are the reader's choice, and with JavaScript off every app's steps stand one under the
    other, which is the page this replaced.

    The apps' marks are drawn single-colour, in ink, from Simple Icons (CC0). §2 draws
    targum's own mark single-colour "everywhere small or third-party", and the same holds
    the other way round: an orange, a blue and a gradient in one row would spend the
    page's whole hue budget on other people's names.

    Baked in like every public page — no script, stylesheet, font or image off the
    network (§11). `connect.js` makes the conversation and the set-up screens move, and
    copies the address. Nothing here needs it. -#}
